WEBVTT

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.550
<i>Thirty-five years ago,</i>

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.100
<i>a brand new continent</i>
<i>appeared out of thin air.</i>

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.310
<i>Lush with new species of flora and fauna,</i>

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.350
<i>as well as mineral resources,</i>

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.110
<i>this continent of endless possibilities</i>

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.980
<i>was dubbed, Magmell.</i>

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.360
<i>Driven wild with ambition,</i>

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.160
<i>explorers came in droves to Magmell</i>

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.160
<i>in hopes of striking it rich.</i>

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.510
Seems we're surrounded.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.760
All the better.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.390
Let's test out our new skills!

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.730
I'll become...

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.570
the king of this age of exploration!

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.040
<i>Sir, they're over here.</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:30.850
So they were wiped out?

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.890
<i>A search and rescue specialist.</i>

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.890
<i>Jurisdiction: Magmell.</i>

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.730
<i>People like him are called Anglers.</i>

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.790
ANGLER

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:22.040
KUSK ARCHIPELAGO

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.310
Sir, it's noon already.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.320
I think I'm just gonna sleep
until tomorrow comes.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.700
The skies cleared up
and the weather's nice.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.080
A sunny day or a rainy day...

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.710
Which one do you think
has more casualties?

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.590
I'd say a sunny one.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:25.520
So this is where
a top notch Angler lives...

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.810
DRIFT

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.490
I'd wager that the concept
of "no work, no food"

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.820
is just some illusion
that people dreamed up one day.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:41.450
Breakfast today is toast,
with no butter or jam.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:42.870
Why's that?

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.460
Because we have no money.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.670
Well, it's pretty good just toasted.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.210
Come tomorrow we can't even do that.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.130
Why's that?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.960
Because they're shutting off our power.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.430
Then I'll make sure to savor this one.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.520
What's your business?

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.520
I...

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.940
I have a... request...

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:07.850
for you...

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.900
Hey!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:25.500
I wish you'd paid us a visit
when you were in better health...

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.340
I'm sorry. I've had a weak constitution
since I was born.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.170
So, Mr. Kriks, what are you doing here?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.090
How did you...?

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.230
You're pretty well off
for someone so young.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:47.350
So? Why are you here?

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.350
I...

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:53.110
I want to pay you this
to save my big brother, Kunuris.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:54.940
I refuse.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.070
What? Why?

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.490
It's not enough.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.450
I can pay you as much
as you need afterwards--

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:05.580
You'd put a price on
your own brother's life?

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.460
I don't have much longer to live.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.170
There will be insurance money when I die.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.420
You can have that.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.380
So...

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.930
Please...

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.570
I can at least hear you out.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:40.360
My parents were

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.120
explorers who went on a journey
to Magmell, the new continent.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:47.370
<i>I promise,</i>

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.870
<i>we'll find the Tear of Epona</i>
<i>and bring it home with us.</i>

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.130
<i>Don't you worry, Kriks.</i>

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.630
<i>The Tear of Epona is</i>
<i>necessary to cure your illness.</i>

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.140
<i>Kriks, let's go to Magmell together</i>
<i>once you're healed.</i>

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.640
Yeah! Together!

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:35.840
Brother!

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:40.880
Where are father and mother?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:44.800
It's my fault.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.560
Because of me, father and mother...

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.560
Brother...

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:51.730
It wasn't enough.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:53.730
Any of it.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:18.840
That's incredible!

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.470
For someone your age to receive
an A-Class Explorer's License!

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.060
I'll bring back the Tear of Epona,
without fail.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.520
Once I do, let's go to Magmell together.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.480
Yeah, together!

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:54.910
Sir?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.500
Shall we go save your brother now?

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:02.510
As per your request.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.510
But... why all of a sudden?

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.390
The Tear of Epona.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.430
I can sell that for a hefty sum.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.480
First, with this helicopter,
we'll go find your brother

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:22.900
at the Bastion City of the Sixth Ward
near the Bohdoka Mountain Woods.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:26.110
Wait. We're not going
directly to the location?

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:30.120
Magmell rejects foreign objects.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:31.660
Rejects?

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:35.830
We didn't pack any weapons,
and it's much too dangerous by helicopter.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:44.960
Down to business.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.810
SIXTH WARD BASTION CITY
TAIDI

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.020
This is... Magmell?

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.230
From here, we'll take him.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.230
POLNY

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.400
They are one of the few animals
from Magmell that have been domesticated.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.280
Explorers from all over
the world visit this place.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.240
Your life is in your own hands.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.240
Too many people were turning up dead,

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.460
which is why exploration
now requires a license.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.750
Do you have a license too, Mr. Inyo?

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.340
Anglers are an exception.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:26.460
It's an Angler's job
to save explorers in distress.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.760
There is the Bohdoka Mountain Woods
that make up 80 percent of the Sixth Ward.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.140
We'll go on foot from here.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:41.770
They're too scared to go
any further than this.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:45.400
The master...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.650
has probably arrived
at the Bohdoka Mountain Woods by now.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.660
I have to hurry to his side.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:57.540
And?

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.460
Right. The Epona fruit

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.540
has the power to return a body
to its full strength,

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:06.840
and even improve
one's physical abilities tenfold.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:10.840
Do you know why the Epona fruit is called

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:11.840
the Tear of Epona?

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:13.600
No.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.390
The Epona

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.560
only blooms atop a mountain of corpses.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:22.900
If your illness is healed
will you become an explorer too?

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.320
I want to become a Lachter.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:29.320
Lachter?

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:34.240
People who have the ability
to construct physical objects at will.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:38.870
Some people will say
that there's no such thing.

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:40.370
But I believe in them.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:46.540
Sir?

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.800
I'm sorry, Mr. Inyo.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.180
If I could just rest a moment...

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:55.760
Zero...

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:03.900
Eat this. It might make things
a little more bearable.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:09.570
This is one of those highly nutritious
Wolf Radishes, isn't it?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.780
I'll add a surcharge for it.

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.610
We're in a hurry, so eat as you walk.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:17.780
Where did this come from?

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:19.910
By the way,

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.670
<i>Wolf Radishes become deathly poisonous</i>
<i>five minutes after they're picked.</i>

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.010
Mr. Inyo! Someone's there!

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:35.300
Help... me.

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:38.600
Someone... Someone help...

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.560
He's in trouble! We have to help him!

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.230
Go ahead, if you'd like to die.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.450
That's bait.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.700
They intentionally let
the decoy live and make it wander,

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.080
then prey on humans that come close.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.540
It's like a living trap.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:09.880
Terrifying creatures like this exist?

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.880
Magmell's true terror

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.630
is much worse than this.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.890
We can't do anything to help him?

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.810
Not even anything to relieve his pain?

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.680
It's pointless.

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.730
Wouldn't even earn me
the tiniest amount of money.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.420
What's that?

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.550
This sensor is linked to explorer badges.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:59.390
If it's reacting,
that means your brother is alive.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:01.970
Is that true, Mr. Inyo?

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:05.060
Yeah. Your brother is just up ahead.

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:16.280
Sir, there's trouble.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:19.280
There's a Prinz Hawk nest
just ahead of you.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.070
<i>There are over 20 adults.</i>

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.210
Don't move from there.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.120
What?

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.290
Gonna take care of business.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:33.670
Wait, what?

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:02.450
Mr. Inyo!

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:06.370
Brother?

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:10.250
Kriks!

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:28.520
<i>Sir, the rest are fleeing.</i>

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.350
It would seem... that's that.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:34.560
Business sure is hard work.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:48.910
Kriks...

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.540
Do you understand how
dangerous this place is?

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.920
I'm sorry... But I was worried about you.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.630
Take a look.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.310
Is this...?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.360
Yeah. It's an Epona.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:26.950
Are these...?

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.410
Yeah.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:31.120
Why...

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.170
The Epona...

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:36.130
blooms atop corpses.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:37.540
But if that's the case...

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.800
It wasn't enough.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.420
How did this happen?

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.010
Who would do something like this?

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.930
Two dead bodies...

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:54.100
weren't enough.

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:57.860
Brother...?

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:00.110
But...

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:01.860
Why...?

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:04.360
So I gathered allies,

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.610
but it still wasn't enough.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.550
This is...

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.230
Sir.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.610
Who are you?

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.650
Sir?

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.240
Zero, administer first-aid.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.280
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.120
Answer me!

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.080
You killed them, didn't you?

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:55.660
Your parents and your allies.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:57.710
For a thing like that.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:00.920
What would you know?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.500
It's not like his illness
would be completely cured

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:05.920
just by giving him a Tear of Epona.

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:07.510
He'd die eventually.

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:09.140
In which case,

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:12.470
doesn't it hold more value to
a person who still has long to live?

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.810
He risked his life

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:19.810
and tried to save you,
despite being on the verge of death.

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.360
And if he hadn't come here

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:24.690
he might have lived just a bit longer.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.490
<i>Sir, the first-aid treatment is complete.</i>

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.950
<i>But he's already...</i>

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:35.200
Mr. Inyo...

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.710
Save my brother.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:42.710
I'm sure he's being
manipulated by something.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.340
Like that person back in the forest.

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:49.340
Okay, Mr. Inyo?

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.140
I'm just going to die from my illness...

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:57.060
My brother is a fine explorer.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:00.770
<i>He's my hero.</i>

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.230
Save...

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.230
my brother...

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:09.990
I understand.

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:14.660
Mr. Inyo.

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:18.000
I had a lot of fun...

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.290
<i>exploring...</i>

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:22.420
with...

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:23.880
you...

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.520
He finally died--

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:47.900
<i>This is Magmell's true terror.</i>

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:52.450
<i>It amplifies the greed</i>
<i>and hatred within humans.</i>

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.160
You killed your parents.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:58.410
You killed your allies.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.210
In the end,
you even killed your little brother.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.250
You bastard!

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:06.250
<i>There's only one way to save you!</i>

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.550
I'll turn you into Epona fertilizer, too!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.010
That's a nice feeling!

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.250
Damn it!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.210
<i>Lachter?</i>

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:48.750
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:51.460
Once I'm cured, I want to be a Lachter!

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.920
Not an explorer?

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:57.300
I'll become a Lachter and help you out!

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.390
You dummy.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.970
Lachters are just an old folk tale.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:04.770
Lachter!

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:06.270
<i>I'll save you!</i>

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:30.380
<i>Zero...</i>

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.340
<i>I'm glad you're here.</i>

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:36.010
<i>Me too, sir.</i>

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:12.610
PREVIEW

00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:14.820
<i>I showed up here just</i>
<i>as Papa instructed...</i>

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:17.280
<i>But is this really the legendary Angler?</i>

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:19.110
<i>He feels kind of unreliable.</i>

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:22.530
<i>And the assistant next to me</i>
<i>keeps giving me weird looks.</i>

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:24.990
<i>Aren't these two still kids anyway?</i>

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:26.830
<i>They might even be younger than me.</i>

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:29.080
<i>Yet his tone is so condescending.</i>

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:31.460
<i>But all I can do now is believe in Papa...</i>

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:34.170
<i>Am I being glared at again?</i>

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:35.250
<i>Why...?</i>

00:23:36.130 --> 00:23:38.300
<i>Next time,</i>
<i>"The Seventh Ward's Controller."</i>

00:23:38.380 --> 00:23:39.420
<i>I recommend you watch it.</i>

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:41.510
Subtitle translation by Keith McAbee
